# C4-5 (round 19, writer 10): L §4.2 "A schedule that gives no date in the run is refused at load where load sees it
# (LOAD-SCHEDULE, §8.3); where it doesn't, each period whose day doesn't exist gives none": dom is a row, so load
# doesn't see the day; 2026-02 has no day 31, so pay has no instance (L §5.14): no movement, flows 0.00. The old comment:
# L §4.2: "A schedule that gives no date in the run is refused at load (LOAD-SCHEDULE)": day 31 of February 2026
# alone gives none at every key of the move.  (A schedule outside a move's on is not checked: what its run is isn't
# stated, HANDOVER.md.)
=== m.tally
model sch
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
index qm = month 2026-02..2026-02
input dom: int
input amt: money PLN
input cal: calendar

move pay[m in qm]: transfers
  on schedule(m, dom, unadjusted, cal)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dom = 31
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

ask q1: count(x in transfers over 2026), flows(pay, 2026)
ask q2: x.day for x in transfers over 2026
=== expect
q1: (0, 0.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
